  "about": "Shared vectors for the background-check wording list (core/src/harness/fixed/background-wording.json), run by the page (core/test/harness/background-wording.test.ts), the native check (core/native-auth/src/background.rs tests) and ozzie.church (web/test/hosted-parity.test.ts). match: text every side refuses (reviews B and B2 included: possessives, \"is the check in\", invisible blanks between words, Ozzie's own sentence inside other text, characters newer than the page's Unicode data). refused_on_purpose: ordinary text every side refuses anyway because it reads exactly like a background-check question, as v0.1.0 did; on the page it gets the refusal or an answer written on this Mac. pass: text no side may refuse (Ozzie's own sentence as a whole string included). known_misses: wording the list does not catch, kept so the limits stay written down and tested. hidden: wording no folding reads (its invisible or newer characters must be deleted at one point and read as a word break at another), which every route refuses anyway because it holds a character no question may hold: the page (prepareAsk), the native Ask check (agent.rs `hidden_in_question`) and ozzie.church's (`questionCharactersOk`) (review B3 L-1). tool_match and tool_pass: tool results, scanned one string at a time. tokens: [text, folding, words] for each folding (join, split, v010). Fictional names only.",
